    "def-rpm-h-temporal-chart-data": {
      "supplier": "def-rpm-h-temporal-chart-data",
      "status": "draft_unbound",
      "actual_file": "items/def-rpm-h-temporal-chart-data.md",
      "actual_status": "draft",
      "actual_pipeline_run": "absent",
      "actual_frontmatter_parseable": true,
      "actual_domain": "mathematics",
      "actual_proof_provenance": "not-applicable",
      "actual_section": "Definition",
      "actual_statement_excerpt": "Assume countable choice ACω, as in [[def-countable-choice]], for the smooth cotangent-bundle carrier convention used by this page; no full Axiom of Choice is assumed.\n\nLet $(M,g,T)$ be a smooth, time-oriented Lorentzian four-manifold of signature $(-+++)$, with the geometric meaning fixed by [[def-gr-smooth-lorentzian-objects]]. A **temporal product chart** is a smooth coordinate map from an open product $I\\times\\Omega\\subset\\mathbb R\\times\\mathbb R^3$ onto an open subset of $M$, with coordinates $(x^0,x^1,x^2,x^3)$. We require $x^0$ to have length units and each $x^i$ to have length units in the physical interpretation.\n\nThe chart has **lapse-shift data** $(N,\\beta,h)$ when $N:I\\times\\Omega\\to(0,\\infty)$, $\\beta^i:I\\times\\Omega\\to\\mathbb R$, and $h_{ij}:I\\times\\Omega\\to\\mathbb R$ are smooth, $h_{ij}=h_{ji}$, and the matrix $(h_{ij})$ is positive definite at each point, with\n\n$$g=-N^2(dx^0)^2+h_{ij}(dx^i+\\beta^i dx^0)(dx^j+\\beta^j dx^0).$$\n\nWrite $h^{ij}$ for the inverse matrix. The normal field is\n\n$$n=N^{-1}(\\partial_0-\\beta^i\\partial_i).$$\n\nDirect contraction gives $g(n,n)=-1$; require that $n$ is future-directed in the supplied time orientation. This field of observers is distinct from the coordinate vector $\\partial_0$, which may be spacelike. The coefficients $N,\\beta^i,h_{ij}$ are dimensionless when all four coordinates are in metres. This definition is local to the specified product chart; it asserts no global temporal foliation.",
      "actual_dependencies": [
        "def-countable-choice",
        "def-gr-smooth-lorentzian-objects"
      ],
      "planned_source_module": "workers/hamiltonian/mass-shell-and-time-gauges.md#H9",
