    "post-rpm-h-massless-shell-action": {
      "supplier": "post-rpm-h-massless-shell-action",
      "status": "draft_unbound",
      "actual_file": "items/post-rpm-h-massless-shell-action.md",
      "actual_status": "draft",
      "actual_pipeline_run": "absent",
      "actual_frontmatter_parseable": true,
      "actual_domain": "physics",
      "actual_proof_provenance": "not-applicable",
      "actual_section": "Postulate",
      "actual_statement_excerpt": "On a prescribed background $(M,g,T)$, adopt a distinct massless classical particle model with fields $x:I\\to M$, $p(\\lambda)\\in T^*_{x(\\lambda)}M$, and a positive smooth multiplier $e(\\lambda)>0$:\n\n$$S_0[x,p,e]=\\int_I\\left[p_a x'^a-eC_0(x,p)\\right]d\\lambda,\\qquad C_0=\\tfrac12g^{ab}p_ap_b.$$\n\nVariations of $p,e$ are independent; the physical branch is $p\\ne0$, $p^\\sharp$ future null. With all spacetime coordinates measured in metres and dimensionless λ, $p_a$ has units kg m/s, $C_0$ has units kg²m²/s² and $e$ has units s/kg, making the action J s. Other parameter units scale $e$ accordingly. This is a separate adopted model: null curves have no proper-time parameter, the model does not arise by setting $m=0$ in $P=mU$, and its positive momentum scale is additional initial data. On the nonzero branch, $C_0$ is a regular primary constraint in the sense of [[def-rpm-h-regular-constraint-system]]; regularity is checked by the shell theorem. This postulate is not an empirical observation or a deduction from the massive model.\n\nThe cotangent phase-space carrier convention assumes countable choice ACω only; full choice is not assumed.",
