      "actual_proof_provenance": "ai-altered",
      "actual_section": "Statement",
      "actual_statement_excerpt": "Let $Q$ be a finite-dimensional smooth manifold as in [[def-rpm-h-cotangent-phase-space]], and write its cotangent phase space in induced coordinates $(q^i,p_i)$. With $omega=dq^i\\wedge dp_i$, define $X_H$ by $iota_{X_H}omega=dH$ and ${F,G}:=X_G(F)$. Then\n\n$$X_H=\\frac{\\partial H}{\\partial p_i}\\frac{\\partial}{\\partial q^i}-\\frac{\\partial H}{\\partial q^i}\\frac{\\partial}{\\partial p_i},\\qquad \\{F,G\\}=F_{q^i}G_{p_i}-F_{p_i}G_{q^i}.$$\n\nThe bracket is coordinate independent and makes smooth functions a Poisson algebra. If $H_t$ is $C^2$ on an open time-dependent domain $D\\subset\\mathbb R\\times T^*Q$, each solution of $\\dot z=X_{H_t}(z)$ has the local uniqueness and smooth parameter dependence of the ODE theorem; on its actual interval,\n\n$$\\frac{d}{dt}F(t,z(t))=\\partial_tF+\\{F,H_t\\}.$$\n\nNo completeness or global flow is asserted. If $H$ is smooth, each local time-$t$ flow map preserves ω.",
      "actual_dependencies": [
        "def-countable-choice",
        "def-rpm-h-cotangent-phase-space",
        "thm-smooth-functions-form-a-poisson-algebra",
        "thm-smooth-dependence-of-ode-solutions-on-parameters"
      ],
      "planned_source_module": "workers/hamiltonian/geometry-and-constraints.md#H0",
