    "thm-rpm-h-constraint-consistency": {
      "supplier": "thm-rpm-h-constraint-consistency",
      "status": "draft_unbound",
      "actual_file": "items/thm-rpm-h-constraint-consistency.md",
      "actual_status": "draft",
      "actual_pipeline_run": "absent",
      "actual_frontmatter_parseable": true,
      "actual_domain": "mathematics",
      "actual_proof_provenance": "ai-altered",
      "actual_section": "Statement",
      "actual_statement_excerpt": "Let $(P,\\omega)$ be a symplectic manifold, $N=\\{\\chi_1=\\cdots=\\chi_r=0\\}$ a regular level surface, and $H_c$ a smooth ambient extension of a specified descended Hamiltonian. For smooth multipliers $u^a(\\lambda)$, the first-order action\n\n$$I[z,u]=\\int\\left[\\theta(\\dot z)-H_c(z)-u^a\\chi_a(z)\\right]d\\lambda$$\n\nwith fixed endpoints and unrestricted multiplier variations gives $z\\in N$ and $\\dot z=X_{H_c}+u^aX_{\\chi_a}$ on $N$, using $\\iota_{X_H}\\omega=dH$. A trajectory remains in $N$ only when\n\n$$\\partial_\\lambda\\chi_a+\\{\\chi_a,H_c\\}+u^b\\{\\chi_a,\\chi_b\\}=0\\quad\\text{on }N.$$\n\nFor autonomous constraints the first term is zero. This equation is a tangency/consistency condition: it can determine multipliers, leave undetermined directions, produce further constraints, or be inconsistent. It does not assert that an arbitrary algorithm terminates after finitely many steps, that ranks remain constant, or that first-class flows always form a global quotient.",
      "actual_dependencies": [
        "def-countable-choice",
        "def-rpm-h-cotangent-phase-space",
        "def-rpm-h-regular-constraint-system",
        "thm-rpm-h-canonical-poisson-and-flow",
        "thm-darboux-theorem",
        "thm-cm-stationarity-iff-euler-lagrange"
      ],
      "planned_source_module": "workers/hamiltonian/geometry-and-constraints.md#H2",
      "planned_source_section": "H2",
      "planned_proof_status": "complete exact stated argument",
      "planned_scope": "Multiplier variation, Hamilton field tangency, possible secondary constraints/inconsistency; no universal algorithm termination.",
      "readiness_reason": "Draft carrier is unbound to the active run and has no current Step 1 readiness or independent proof approval.",
      "manifest_page": "rpm-hamiltonian-constraints",
      "manifest_item_present": true,
      "manifest_dependencies": [
