    "thm-rpm-h-first-order-action-and-geodesics": {
      "supplier": "thm-rpm-h-first-order-action-and-geodesics",
      "status": "draft_unbound",
      "actual_file": "items/thm-rpm-h-first-order-action-and-geodesics.md",
      "actual_status": "draft",
      "actual_pipeline_run": "absent",
      "actual_frontmatter_parseable": true,
      "actual_domain": "mathematics",
      "actual_proof_provenance": "ai-altered",
      "actual_section": "Statement",
      "actual_statement_excerpt": "Let $(M,g,T)$ be a prescribed smooth time-oriented Lorentzian four-manifold with signature $(-+++)$. For $m\\ge0$ define $C_m=\\tfrac12(g^{ab}p_ap_b+m^2c^2)$ and the first-order functional\n\n$$I_m[x,p,e]=\\int\\left(p_ax'^a-eC_m(x,p)\\right)d\\lambda,\\qquad e>0.$$\n\nTake independent smooth variations of $p,e$ and fixed-endpoint variations of $x$. Stationarity is equivalent to\n\n$$x'^a=e g^{ab}p_b,\\quad p'_a=-\\tfrac e2\\partial_a g^{bc}p_bp_c,\\quad C_m=0.$$\n\nOn the massive future branch $m>0$, these equations are equivalent to stationary paths of the square-root action in [[post-rpm-h-free-test-particle-action]]; the mechanical covector is (p=mc\\,x'^\\flat/\\sqrt{-g(x',x')}), and proper-time gauge has $e=1/m$. For the separate nonzero future-null branch $m=0$, the equations describe a null geodesic with an arbitrary positive parameter multiplier; no proper-time parameter exists. In both cases the unparameterized path is a geodesic, and no existence or completeness claim is made.",
      "actual_dependencies": [
        "def-countable-choice",
        "def-rpm-h-background-and-model-quantities",
        "def-rpm-h-cotangent-phase-space",
