    "thm-rpm-h-inertial-time-reduced-hamiltonian": {
      "supplier": "thm-rpm-h-inertial-time-reduced-hamiltonian",
      "status": "draft_unbound",
      "actual_file": "items/thm-rpm-h-inertial-time-reduced-hamiltonian.md",
      "actual_status": "draft",
      "actual_pipeline_run": "absent",
      "actual_frontmatter_parseable": true,
      "actual_domain": "mathematics",
      "actual_proof_provenance": "ai-altered",
      "actual_section": "Statement",
      "actual_statement_excerpt": "In affine Minkowski space with $x^0=ct$, let $m\\ge0$, $p_i$ be spatial momentum components and $p_i\\ne0$ for $m=0$. On the future shell, $p_0=-E/c$, where\n\n$$E(\\mathbf p)=\\sqrt{m^2c^4+c^2|\\mathbf p|^2}.$$\n\nThe gauge $x^0=ct$ reduces the first-order shell action to\n\n$$I=\\int\\left(p_i\\dot q^i-E(\\mathbf p)\\right)dt,\\qquad q^i=x^i.$$\n\nThe gauge pair $C_m=0$, $\\psi=x^0-ct=0$ is second class because $\\{C_m,\\psi\\}=-P^0\\ne0$ on the future shell; its Dirac reduction gives the canonical spatial bracket. The reduced Hamilton equations are $\\dot q^i=c^2p_i/E$, $\\dot p_i=0$, agreeing with the unreduced characteristic trajectories. On this full flat future shell every characteristic line meets each inertial-time slice once; this global assertion does not extend by this proof to a curved temporal chart.",
      "actual_dependencies": [
