      "actual_frontmatter_parseable": true,
      "actual_domain": "mathematics",
      "actual_proof_provenance": "ai-altered",
      "actual_section": "Statement",
      "actual_statement_excerpt": "Assume a temporal product chart with lapse-shift data $(N,\\beta,h)$ as in [[def-rpm-h-temporal-chart-data]], all four coordinates measured in metres. On the future shell $C_m=\\tfrac12(g^{ab}p_ap_b+m^2c^2)=0$, define\n\n$$\\kappa=\\sqrt{m^2c^2+h^{ij}p_ip_j},\\quad p_0=\\beta^ip_i-N\\kappa,\\quad H(t,q,p)=-cp_0=c(N\\kappa-\\beta^ip_i).$$\n\nFor $m=0$, require $p_i\\ne0$. On every path interval contained in the chart, the gauge $x^0=ct$ reduces the first-order action to $\\int(p_i\\dot q^i-H)dt$, and its variational equations are exactly $\\dot q^i=H_{p_i}$, $\\dot p_i=-H_{q^i}$. The construction is local to this chart and to intervals transverse to its time slices.",
      "actual_dependencies": [
        "def-countable-choice",
