          "id": "step-5-1",
          "claim": "Antisymmetry of $A^{bc}$ gives $J_{bc}A^{bc}=-2p_bA^b{}_cx^c$: expand $J_{bc}=x_bp_c-x_cp_b$ and interchange $b,c$ in the first term. Substitution yields $\\ell=p_ba^b-\\tfrac12J_{bc}A^{bc}$. The definitions of $P,J$ then give $[P^a]=\\mathrm{kg\\,m/s}$ and $[J^{ab}]=\\mathrm{J\\,s}$ from $[x]=\\mathrm m$, $[p]=\\mathrm{kg\\,m/s}$, and $[c]=\\mathrm{m/s}$.",
          "step": "5.1",
