          "current_carrier": "items/thm-rpm-h-homogeneous-massive-shell.md",
          "actual_kind": "theorem",
          "actual_sha256": "a3102e26b1e19a79fb00ce48c3979f4cc73ac4ab74bfa0f07d9be165b5346045",
          "actual_source_section": "Statement",
          "actual_step1_decision": "ready",
          "actual_step1_hash_current": true
        },
        {
          "supplier": "thm-rpm-h-inertial-time-reduced-hamiltonian",
          "status": "draft_unbound",
          "actual_file": "items/thm-rpm-h-inertial-time-reduced-hamiltonian.md",
          "actual_status": "draft",
          "actual_pipeline_run": "absent",
          "actual_frontmatter_parseable": true,
          "actual_domain": "mathematics",
          "actual_proof_provenance": "ai-altered",
          "actual_section": "Statement",
          "actual_statement_excerpt": "In affine Minkowski space with $x^0=ct$, let $m\\ge0$, $p_i$ be spatial momentum components and $p_i\\ne0$ for $m=0$. On the future shell, $p_0=-E/c$, where\n\n$$E(\\mathbf p)=\\sqrt{m^2c^4+c^2|\\mathbf p|^2}.$$\n\nOn any compact interval $J=[t_1,t_2]$ of inertial time, the gauge $x^0=ct$ reduces the first-order shell action to\n\n$$I_J=\\int_{t_1}^{t_2}\\left(p_i\\dot q^i-E(\\mathbf p)\\right)dt,\\qquad q^i=x^i.$$\n\nThe gauge pair $C_m=0$, $\\psi=x^0-ct=0$ is second class because $\\{C_m,\\psi\\}=-P^0\\ne0$ on the future shell; its Dirac reduction gives the canonical spatial bracket. The reduced Hamilton equations are $\\dot q^i=c^2p_i/E$, $\\dot p_i=0$, agreeing with the unreduced characteristic trajectories. On this full flat future shell every characteristic line meets each inertial-time slice once; this global assertion does not extend by this proof to a curved temporal chart.",
          "actual_dependencies": [
            "def-countable-choice",
            "def-rpm-h-cotangent-phase-space",
