        {
          "supplier": "thm-rpm-h-flat-shell-global-reduction",
          "status": "draft_unbound",
          "actual_file": "items/thm-rpm-h-flat-shell-global-reduction.md",
          "actual_status": "draft",
          "actual_pipeline_run": "absent",
          "actual_frontmatter_parseable": true,
          "actual_domain": "mathematics",
          "actual_proof_provenance": "ai-altered",
          "actual_section": "Statement",
          "actual_statement_excerpt": "In affine Minkowski space with inertial coordinates $x^0,x^i$ measured in metres and metric $\\eta=\\operatorname{diag}(-1,1,1,1)$, let $m\\ge0$ and let\n\n$$\\Sigma_m^+=\\{(x,p): -p_0=P^0=\\sqrt{m^2c^2+|\\mathbf p|^2},\\ p_0<0\\},$$\n\nwhere $\\mathbf p\\ne0$ when $m=0$, and write $P^i=p_i$ for the spatial raised momentum components. The characteristic flow of the restricted canonical form is $(x,p)\\mapsto(x+\\alpha P,p)$, and its orbit space is globally diffeomorphic to $B_m=\\mathbb R^3_a\\times\\mathbb R^3_p$ for $m>0$, or $\\mathbb R^3_a\\times(\\mathbb R^3_p\\setminus\\{0\\})$ for $m=0$, by\n\n$$a^i=x^i-\\frac{P^i}{P^0}x^0,\\qquad p_i=p_i.$$\n\nThe reduced symplectic form is $da^i\\wedge dp_i$. The quotient is Hausdorff and second countable and each full characteristic line meets each slice $x^0=ct$ exactly once. This is an explicit free flat quotient, not a conclusion about arbitrary first-class systems.",
