        {
          "supplier": "def-rpm-h-regular-constraint-system",
          "status": "draft_unbound",
          "actual_file": "items/def-rpm-h-regular-constraint-system.md",
          "actual_status": "draft",
          "actual_pipeline_run": "absent",
          "actual_frontmatter_parseable": true,
          "actual_domain": "mathematics",
          "actual_proof_provenance": "not-applicable",
          "actual_section": "Definition",
          "actual_statement_excerpt": "Assume $\\mathrm{AC}_{\\omega}$ and let $(M^{2n},\\omega)$ be a smooth symplectic manifold. A finite family of smooth functions $\\chi_1,\\ldots,\\chi_r$ defined on an open neighborhood $U\\subseteq M$ is a **regular primary constraint family** on\n\n$$C:=\\{z\\in U:\\chi_1(z)=\\cdots=\\chi_r(z)=0\\}$$\n\nwhen $d\\chi_1(z),\\ldots,d\\chi_r(z)$ are linearly independent at every $z\\in C$. The regular-level theorem [[thm-a-regular-level-set-is-an-embedded-submanifold]] then gives $C$ its embedded-submanifold structure and $T_zC=\\bigcap_a\\ker d\\chi_a(z)$. For functions $F,G$ on $U$, write $F\\approx G$ when $F|_C=G|_C$; thus $F\\approx0$ means that $F$ vanishes on $C$, without requiring it to vanish off $C$.\n\nGiven a smooth canonical Hamiltonian $H_c$ on $U$ and multiplier functions $u^a(t)$, the **total generator** is\n\n$$H_T(t,z):=H_c(t,z)+\\sum_{a=1}^r u^a(t)\\chi_a(z).$$\n\nThe functions $u^a$ are independent parameter functions; the definition does not assert that their equations determine them. If $H_c$ is an energy and $\\chi_a$ has units \\([\\chi_a]\\), then $u^a$ has units energy divided by \\([\\chi_a]\\), so every term in $H_T$ has the same units. A later constraint, if generated by consistency, is not declared primary by this definition.",
          "actual_dependencies": [
            "def-countable-choice",
            "def-rpm-h-cotangent-phase-space",
            "def-symplectic-form-and-symplectic-manifold",
            "thm-a-regular-level-set-is-an-embedded-submanifold"
          ],
          "planned_source_module": "workers/hamiltonian/geometry-and-constraints.md#H2",
