        {
          "supplier": "thm-rpm-h-canonical-poisson-and-flow",
          "status": "draft_unbound",
          "actual_file": "items/thm-rpm-h-canonical-poisson-and-flow.md",
          "actual_status": "draft",
          "actual_pipeline_run": "absent",
          "actual_frontmatter_parseable": true,
          "actual_domain": "mathematics",
          "actual_proof_provenance": "ai-altered",
          "actual_section": "Statement",
          "actual_statement_excerpt": "Let $Q$ be a finite-dimensional smooth manifold as in [[def-rpm-h-cotangent-phase-space]], and write its cotangent phase space in induced coordinates $(q^i,p_i)$. With $\\omega=dq^i\\wedge dp_i$, define $X_H$ by $\\iota_{X_H}\\omega=dH$ and define the Poisson bracket by $\\{F,G\\}:=X_G(F)$. Then\n\n$$X_H=\\frac{\\partial H}{\\partial p_i}\\frac{\\partial}{\\partial q^i}-\\frac{\\partial H}{\\partial q^i}\\frac{\\partial}{\\partial p_i},\\qquad \\{F,G\\}=F_{q^i}G_{p_i}-F_{p_i}G_{q^i}.$$\n\nThe bracket is coordinate independent and makes smooth functions a Poisson algebra. If $H_t$ is smooth on an open time-dependent domain $D\\subset\\mathbb R\\times T^*Q$, each solution of $\\dot z=X_{H_t}(z)$ has local uniqueness and smooth dependence on initial data and parameters; on its actual interval,\n\n$$\\frac{d}{dt}F(t,z(t))=\\partial_tF+\\{F,H_t\\}.$$\n\nNo completeness or global flow is asserted. If $H$ is smooth, each local time-$t$ flow map preserves ω.",
          "actual_dependencies": [
