          "quote": "Let $(M,g,T)$ be a prescribed smooth time-oriented Lorentzian four-manifold with signature $(-+++)$. Work in a spacetime chart on a compact parameter interval $[a,b]$ with $a<b$; take $x,p,e$ smooth on a neighbourhood of that interval, $e>0$, $m\\ge0$, and $c>0$. Select stationary triples on the future shell branch after taking the independent variations: when $m>0$, $p^\\sharp$ is future timelike; when $m=0$, require $p\\ne0$ and $p^\\sharp$ future null. Set $C_m=\\tfrac12(g^{ab}p_ap_b+m^2c^2)$ and define the first-order functional\n\n$$I_m[x,p,e]=\\int_a^b\\left(p_ax'^a-eC_m(x,p)\\right)d\\lambda.$$\n\nTake independent smooth variations of $p,e$ and fix",
