          "claim": "In coordinates, $\\partial_{x^c}F_\\xi=p_a\\partial_c\\xi^a$, $\\partial_{p_c}F_\\xi=\\xi^c$, $\\partial_{p_c}C_m=g^{cb}p_b$, and $\\partial_{x^c}C_m=\\tfrac12\\partial_cg^{ab}p_ap_b$. Therefore [L2] gives $\\{F_\\xi,C_m\\}=p_a(\\partial_c\\xi^a)g^{cb}p_b-\\tfrac12\\xi^c(\\partial_cg^{ab})p_ap_b=-\\tfrac12(\\mathcal L_\\xi g^{-1})^{ab}p_ap_b,$ by the coordinate definition $(\\mathcal L_\\xi g^{-1})^{ab}=\\xi^c\\partial_cg^{ab}-g^{cb}\\partial_c\\xi^a-g^{ac}\\partial_c\\xi^b$ and symmetry of $p_ap_b$.",
