        },
        {
          "supplier": "post-rpm-h-free-test-particle-action",
          "status": "draft_unbound",
          "actual_file": "items/post-rpm-h-free-test-particle-action.md",
          "actual_status": "draft",
          "actual_pipeline_run": "absent",
          "actual_frontmatter_parseable": true,
          "actual_domain": "physics",
          "actual_proof_provenance": "not-applicable",
          "actual_section": "Postulate",
          "actual_statement_excerpt": "For a $C^2$ future-directed timelike worldline $x:I\\to M$ on a prescribed smooth, time-oriented Lorentzian background $(M,g,T)$ of signature $(-+++)$, with $m>0$ a fixed primitive mass in kg and $c>0$ in m/s, adopt the stationary-action model\n\n$$S_m[x]=-mc\\int_I\\sqrt{-g(x',x') }\\,d\\lambda.$$\n\nHere λ is an increasing regular parameter, endpoint events are fixed, and admissible variations remain future timelike. The integrand is the proper-time length density, so $S_m=-mc^2\\int d\\tau$; its dimension is action (J s). The adopted premise concerns this ideal free test body only. It is neither a theorem about all matter nor an empirical report, and supplies no backreaction or completeness claim. The flat ideal-clock specialization agrees with [[post-sr-ideal-clocks-and-light]]; adopting this action on a curved background remains a separate premise.\n\nThe cotangent phase-space carrier convention assumes countable choice ACω only; full choice is not assumed.",
