          "actual_domain": "mathematics",
          "actual_proof_provenance": "ai-altered",
          "actual_section": "Statement",
          "actual_statement_excerpt": "Let $(P,\\omega)$ be symplectic and let $\\chi_1,\\ldots,\\chi_{2k}$ be smooth on an open set $U$, with $C_{ab}=\\{\\chi_a,\\chi_b\\}$ invertible at every point of $U$. Write $C^{ab}$ for its inverse and $N=\\{\\chi=0\\}\\cap U$. Then $N$ is an embedded symplectic submanifold, and the bracket\n\n$$\\{F,G\\}_D=\\{F,G\\}-\\{F,\\chi_a\\}C^{ab}\\{\\chi_b,G\\}$$\n\nis the Poisson bracket of the restricted symplectic form on $N$. It is independent of ambient extensions of $F,G$, and every $\\chi_a$ is a Casimir. This is local and assumes invertibility on $U$; it does not cover singular points.",
          "actual_dependencies": [
            "def-countable-choice",
            "def-rpm-h-regular-constraint-system",
            "def-symplectic-form-and-symplectic-manifold",
            "thm-a-regular-level-set-is-an-embedded-submanifold",
            "thm-smooth-functions-form-a-poisson-algebra"
