          "actual_domain": "mathematics",
          "actual_proof_provenance": "ai-altered",
          "actual_section": "Statement",
          "actual_statement_excerpt": "Let $L(q,v)$ be $C^2$ on a conic open subset of a tangent bundle, and suppose $L(q,av)=aL(q,v)$ for every $a>0$ in its domain. At each nonzero $v$,\n\n$$v^iL_{v^i}=L,\\qquad L_{v^iv^j}v^i=0,\\qquad E_L:=v^iL_{v^i}-L=0.$$\n\nConsequently the velocity Hessian is singular and the fibre derivative cannot be a local diffeomorphism there; a regular Legendre equivalence theorem cannot be applied. These conclusions do not imply that the motion is static or that the Lagrangian has a specified constraint surface.",
