        },
        {
          "supplier": "thm-rpm-h-homogeneous-massive-shell",
          "status": "draft_unbound",
          "actual_file": "items/thm-rpm-h-homogeneous-massive-shell.md",
          "actual_status": "draft",
          "actual_pipeline_run": "absent",
          "actual_frontmatter_parseable": true,
          "actual_domain": "mathematics",
          "actual_proof_provenance": "ai-altered",
          "actual_section": "Statement",
          "actual_statement_excerpt": "Let $(M,g,T)$ be a smooth time-oriented Lorentzian four-manifold, $m>0$, and $L(x,V)=-mc\\sqrt{-g(V,V)}$ on the future timelike tangent cone. Its fibre derivative is\n\n$$p_a=mc\\frac{g_{ab}V^b}{s},\\qquad s=\\sqrt{-g(V,V)}>0.$$\n\nThe velocity Hessian is $mc(g_{ab}/s+V_aV_b/s^3)$, has kernel exactly $\\mathbb RV$, and rank three. The image consists exactly of the future shell $\\Sigma_m^+=\\{(x,p)\\in T^*M:g_x^{-1}(p,p)=-m^2c^2,\\ p^\\sharp\\text{ future}\\}$. Each fibre is a connected positive ray, and the Legendre map is a surjective submersion onto this embedded image. Its energy $p(V)-L$ is zero; the map has no local inverse in the four-velocity direction.",
          "actual_dependencies": [
