    "cex-rpm-h-instantaneous-potential-free-boost": {
      "citations": [
        {
          "fact": "A1",
          "source": "def-countable-choice",
          "source_section": "Definition",
          "quote": "The **Axiom of Countable Choice**, written $\\mathrm{AC}_\\omega$, is the following\nstatement.\n\n> For every family $(X_n)_{n \\in \\mathbb{N}}$ of nonempty sets indexed by\n> $\\mathbb{N}$ there is a function $f$ with domain $\\mathbb{N}$ such that\n> $f(n) \\in X_n$ for every $n \\in \\mathbb{N}$.\n\nEquivalently, in the vocabulary of [[def-choice-function]]: every at most\ncountable family of nonempty sets ([[def-countable]]) has a choice function.",
          "uses": [
            "1.1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "L1",
          "source": "thm-rpm-h-poincare-moment-map-and-algebra",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Assume $\\mathrm{AC}_\\omega$. For the group and cotangent conventions of [[def-rpm-h-poincare-charge-space]], the map $\\mu:T^*\\mathbb R^4\\to\\mathfrak g^*$ defined by $\\langle\\mu(x,p),(a,A)\\rangle=\\ell_{(a,A)}(x,p)$ is a smooth equivariant moment map and obeys\n\n$$\\{\\ell_\\xi,\\ell_\\eta\\}=\\ell_{[\\xi,\\eta]},\\quad \\{P^a,P^b\\}=0,\\quad \\{J^{ab},P^c\\}=\\eta^{ac}P^b-\\eta^{bc}P^a,$$\n\n$$\\{J^{ab},J^{cd}\\}=\\eta^{ac}J^{bd}-\\eta^{ad}J^{bc}-\\eta^{bc}J^{ad}+\\eta^{bd}J^{ac}.$$\n\nFor each future massive shell $p_0=-E/c$, $E=\\sqrt{m^2c^4+c^2|\\mathbf p|^2}$, or nonzero future null shell with $m=0$ and $|\\mathbf p|>0$, its Poincare charges descend to the global ray quotient. The induced dual action is $(P,J)\\mapsto(\\Lambda P,\\Lambda J\\Lambda^T+a\\wedge\\Lambda P)$. On the fixed-time slice $x^0=ct$, with physical position $q^i=x^i$, the boost component $B_i=J^{0i}=ct p_i-q^iE/c$ is explicitly time dependent and satisfies $\\partial_tB_i+\\{B_i,E\\}=0$. These are mathematical identities; conservation is conditional on the stated free-shell evolution.",
          "uses": [
            "1.1",
            "2.1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "F1",
          "source": "def-rpm-h-poincare-charge-space",
          "source_section": "Definition",
          "quote": "Assume $\\mathrm{AC}_\\omega$ for the referenced cotangent and symplectic-action conventions. Work on affine Minkowski spacetime with inertial coordinates $x^0=ct,x^1,x^2,x^3$ in metres, metric matrix $\\eta=\\operatorname{diag}(-1,1,1,1)$, and cotangent coordinates $(x^a,p_a)$, where each $p_a$ has SI momentum units. Fix the future cone as the timelike component containing the positive $x^0$ axis, equivalently $v^0>\\lvert\\mathbf v\\rvert$. Let $SO^+(1,3)$ denote the determinant-one, future-cone-preserving Lorentz subgroup. Define the proper orthochronous Poincaré group and its multiplication by\n\n$$G=\\mathbb R^4\\rtimes SO^+(1,3),\\qquad (a,\\Lambda)(b,L)=(a+\\Lambda b,\\Lambda L).$$\n\nIts action on spacetime and the cotangent lift are $x'=\\Lambda x+a$ and $p'=\\Lambda^{-T}p$. The Lie algebra consists of pairs $(a,A)$ with $A^T\\eta+\\eta A=0$, bracket\n\n$$[(a,A),(b,B)]=(Ab-Ba,[A,B]).$$\n\nUse the library convention $\\xi_M=\\left.\\frac d{ds}\\right|_0\\exp_G(-s\\xi)\\cdot z$. Thus the positive affine generator on spacetime is $Y_{(a,A)}(x)=a+Ax$, the fundamental field is its negative, and the cotangent-lifted positive field is $(a+Ax,-A^Tp)$. Pair the cotangent point with a Lie-algebra element by\n\n$$\\ell_{(a,A)}(x,p)=p_b(a^b+A^b{}_cx^c).$$\n\nDefine $P^a=\\eta^{ab}p_b$ and $J^{ab}=x^aP^b-x^bP^a$. The equivalent dual pairing is $\\ell_{(a,A)}=p_ba^b-\\tfrac12J_{bc}A^{bc}$, where $A^{bc}=A^b{}_d\\eta^{dc}$ and $J_{bc}=\\eta_{bd}\\eta_{ce}J^{de}$. Here $[P^a]=\\mathrm{kg\\,m/s}$ and $[J^{ab}]=\\mathrm{J\\,s}$. These are charge-space definitions on the full cotangent bundle; shell reduction and the moment-map identities are stated separately. No spin or particle model is included.",
          "uses": [
            "1.1"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "derivations": [
        {
          "id": "step-1-1",
          "claim": "By the canonical product bracket, $\\{q_aE_a,p_1+p_2\\}=E_a$ for each $a$, since $E_a$ is independent of position; also $\\{t(p_1+p_2),p_1+p_2\\}=0$. Hence $\\{K,P\\}=(E_1+E_2)/c^2$.",
          "step": "1.1",
          "inputs": [
            "F1",
            "L1",
            "A1",
            "algebra"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "step-2-1",
          "claim": "The Hamiltonian is $H=E_1+E_2+kr^2/2$, so $H/c^2-\\{K,P\\}=kr^2/(2c^2)>0$ whenever $r=q_1-q_2\\ne0$. The required algebra relation in [L1] fails there. Since $k$ has units $\\mathrm{kg/s^2}$, $kr^2/2$ is energy and the compared charges have matching units. This refutes this proposed free-boost construction only.",
          "step": "2.1",
          "inputs": [
            "L1",
            "step 1.1",
            "algebra"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "routine_steps": [],
      "boundaries": [
