        },
        {
          "case": "iff-forward",
          "status": "not_applicable",
          "reason": "Statement refuted — Free boost plus instantaneous relativistic pair potential violates the charge algebra: These conditional identities or constructions do not assert an additional biconditional beyond their stated formulation. The harmonic pair potential has k>0 and positive massive free energies; the fixed free boost misses the potential term whenever the separation is nonzero. Equal positions only remove that discrepancy at one configuration."
        },
