        {
          "supplier": "thm-rpm-h-first-class-local-reduction",
          "status": "draft_unbound",
          "actual_file": "items/thm-rpm-h-first-class-local-reduction.md",
          "actual_status": "draft",
          "actual_pipeline_run": "absent",
          "actual_frontmatter_parseable": true,
          "actual_domain": "mathematics",
          "actual_proof_provenance": "ai-altered",
          "actual_section": "Statement",
          "actual_statement_excerpt": "Let $(P^{2n},\\omega)$ be symplectic, and let $N=\\{\\chi_1=\\cdots=\\chi_r=0\\}$ be a regular embedded level surface with $\\{\\chi_a,\\chi_b\\}=0$ on $N$. Then $\\ker(\\omega|_N)$ is exactly the rank-$r$ distribution spanned by the restricted Hamiltonian vector fields $X_{\\chi_a}$. This distribution is involutive. Around every point of $N$, its leaves admit smooth Frobenius coordinates $(s^1,\\ldots,s^r,y^1,\\ldots,y^{2n-2r})$, and the local leaf space has a unique smooth closed nondegenerate two-form $\\omega_{\\mathrm{red}}$ whose pullback is $\\omega|_N$. Thus regular first-class constraints yield a local symplectic quotient. No global orbit-space regularity follows from these hypotheses.",
