          "actual_statement_excerpt": "Let $I\\subset\\mathbb R$ be an open interval and $(P,\\omega)$ a symplectic manifold. Let $\\chi_a:I\\times P\\to\\mathbb R$ be smooth and suppose the covectors $d_z\\chi_a(\\lambda,z)$ are linearly independent at every $z\\in N_\\lambda:=\\{z:\\chi_1(\\lambda,z)=\\cdots=\\chi_r(\\lambda,z)=0\\}$; this is the regular constraint condition of [[def-rpm-h-regular-constraint-system]] on each slice. Let $H_c:I\\times P\\to\\mathbb R$ be a smooth ambient extension of a specified descended Hamiltonian. Work in a Darboux chart with coordinates $(q^i,p_i)$ and local potential $\\theta=p_i\\,dq^i$, so $d\\theta=-\\omega$ under the convention $\\omega=dq^i\\wedge dp_i$; paths stay in this chart.\nFor any compact interval $[a,b]\\subset I$ with $a<b$, paths $z:[a,b]\\to P$ that stay in the chart and smooth multipliers $u^a:[a,b]\\to\\mathbb R$ have action\n\n$$I[z,u]=\\int_a^b\\left[\\theta(\\dot z)-H_c(\\lambda,z)-u^a(\\lambda)\\chi_a(\\lambda,z)\\right]d\\lambda.$$\n\nFixed-endpoint variations of $z$ and unrestricted variations of $u$ imply $z(\\lambda)\\in N_\\lambda$ and $\\dot z=X_{H_c(\\lambda,\\cdot)}+u^a(\\lambda)X_{\\chi_a(\\lambda,\\cdot)}$. A trajectory remains in the moving level set only when\n\n$$\\partial_\\lambda\\chi_a+\\{\\chi_a,H_c(\\lambda,\\cdot)\\}+u^b(\\lambda)\\{\\chi_a,\\chi_b\\}=0\\quad\\text{on }N_\\lambda.$$\n\nFor constraints independent of $\\lambda$, the first term is zero.",
