        {
          "supplier": "def-rpm-h-cotangent-phase-space",
          "status": "draft_unbound",
          "actual_file": "items/def-rpm-h-cotangent-phase-space.md",
          "actual_status": "draft",
          "actual_pipeline_run": "absent",
          "actual_frontmatter_parseable": true,
          "actual_domain": "mathematics",
          "actual_proof_provenance": "not-applicable",
          "actual_section": "Definition",
          "actual_statement_excerpt": "Assume countable choice $\\mathrm{AC}_{\\omega}$: every sequence of nonempty sets has a choice function ([[def-countable-choice]]). Let $Q$ be a finite-dimensional, Hausdorff, second-countable smooth manifold without boundary, of dimension $n$. Its cotangent bundle is\n\n$$T^*Q=\\coprod_{q\\in Q}T_q^*Q,\\qquad \\pi:T^*Q\\to Q,\\quad \\pi(q,p)=q,$$\n\nwith the canonical smooth structure and induced cotangent charts supplied by the manifold construction in [[def-tautological-one-form-on-a-cotangent-bundle]]. The **tautological one-form** is $\\theta_{(q,p)}(\\xi)=p(d\\pi_{(q,p)}\\xi)$, and the **canonical cotangent two-form** is $\\omega=-d\\theta$. The exact theorem [[thm-the-canonical-cotangent-two-form-is-symplectic]] makes $(T^*Q,\\omega)$ a symplectic manifold in the sense of [[def-symplectic-form-and-symplectic-manifold]]. We call this pair the **cotangent phase space** of $Q$.\n\nIn an induced chart $(q^1,\\ldots,q^n,p_1,\\ldots,p_n)$, $\\theta=p_i\\,dq^i$ and $\\omega=dq^i\\wedge dp_i$. A mathematical **observable** on this phase space means a smooth function $F:T^*Q\\to\\mathbb R$; this definition does not assert that a measurement has been performed or that every such function is physically measurable.\n\nFor an interpreted particle model, assign coordinates $q^i$ their declared units and assign the conjugate covector components $p_i$ units of action divided by the units of $q^i$. Thus $\\theta$ and $\\omega$ have action units, conventionally joule-seconds, and a bracket of quantities with units \\([F]\\) and \\([G]\\) has units \\([F][G]/(\\text{action})\\). These are dimensional interpretations of the model, not additional mathematical premises. The use of $\\mathrm{AC}_{\\omega}$ is exactly the use in the smooth cotangent-bundle suppliers; no full Axiom of Choice is used.",
          "actual_dependencies": [
            "def-countable-choice",
            "def-symplectic-form-and-symplectic-manifold",
            "def-tautological-one-form-on-a-cotangent-bundle",
            "thm-the-canonical-cotangent-two-form-is-symplectic"
          ],
