    "ex-rpm-h-free-relativistic-complete-integral": {
      "citations": [
        {
          "fact": "A1",
          "source": "def-countable-choice",
          "source_section": "Definition",
          "quote": "The **Axiom of Countable Choice**, written $\\mathrm{AC}_\\omega$, is the following\nstatement.\n\n> For every family $(X_n)_{n \\in \\mathbb{N}}$ of nonempty sets indexed by\n> $\\mathbb{N}$ there is a function $f$ with domain $\\mathbb{N}$ such that\n> $f(n) \\in X_n$ for every $n \\in \\mathbb{N}$.\n\nEquivalently, in the vocabulary of [[def-choice-function]]: every at most\ncountable family of nonempty sets ([[def-countable]]) has a choice function.",
          "uses": [
            "1.1",
            "1.2"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "L1",
          "source": "thm-rpm-h-complete-integral-coordinates",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Assume $\\mathrm{AC}_\\omega$ for the cotangent/HJ supplier chain. Let $H(t,q,p)$ be smooth and let $S(t,q,\\alpha)$ be a $C^3$ solution of $S_t+H(t,q,S_q)=0$ on an open domain. If the mixed matrix $S_{q\\alpha}$ is invertible at $(t,q,\\alpha)$, then after restricting neighborhoods the equations $p=S_q$, $\\beta=S_\\alpha$ define a local canonical transformation $(q,p)\\leftrightarrow(\\alpha,\\beta)$ at each fixed $t$, and $\\beta$ is constant along its Hamilton characteristics. Such a family is a complete integral only on that nonsingular local domain. In a temporal spacetime chart satisfying H9, the covariant future-shell equation $g^{ab}S_aS_b+m^2c^2=0$ reduces to the time Hamilton–Jacobi equation with $p_0=S_t/c=-H/c$; for $m=0$ require a nonzero future null covector. The function $S$ has action units, not dimensionless phase units.",
          "uses": [
            "1.1",
            "1.2"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "L2",
          "source": "thm-rpm-h-inertial-time-reduced-hamiltonian",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "In affine Minkowski space with $x^0=ct$, let $m\\ge0$, $p_i$ be spatial momentum components and $p_i\\ne0$ for $m=0$. On the future shell, $p_0=-E/c$, where\n\n$$E(\\mathbf p)=\\sqrt{m^2c^4+c^2|\\mathbf p|^2}.$$\n\nOn any compact interval $J=[t_1,t_2]$ of inertial time, the gauge $x^0=ct$ reduces the first-order shell action to\n\n$$I_J=\\int_{t_1}^{t_2}\\left(p_i\\dot q^i-E(\\mathbf p)\\right)dt,\\qquad q^i=x^i.$$\n\nThe gauge pair $C_m=0$, $\\psi=x^0-ct=0$ is second class because $\\{C_m,\\psi\\}=-P^0\\ne0$ on the future shell; its Dirac reduction gives the canonical spatial bracket. The reduced Hamilton equations are $\\dot q^i=c^2p_i/E$, $\\dot p_i=0$, agreeing with the unreduced characteristic trajectories. On this full flat future shell every characteristic line meets each inertial-time slice once; this global assertion does not extend by this proof to a curved temporal chart.",
          "uses": [
            "1.1",
            "1.2"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "derivations": [
        {
          "id": "step-1-1",
          "claim": "Differentiation gives $S_q=\\alpha$, $S_t=-E(\\alpha)$, and hence $S_t+E(S_q)=0$. Also $S_{q_i\\alpha_j}=\\delta_{ij}$, so its determinant is one. By [L1] this nonsingular family supplies local canonical integration coordinates on the stated domain.",
          "step": "1.1",
          "inputs": [
            "L1",
            "L2",
            "A1",
            "algebra"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "step-1-2",
          "claim": "Differentiating $E$ gives $\\partial_{\\alpha_i}E=c^2\\alpha_i/E$ wherever $E>0$. Thus $\\beta=S_\\alpha=q-tc^2\\alpha/E$ and rearranging yields the stated trajectory formula. For $m=0$, $E=c|\\alpha|>0$ and differentiability requires $\\alpha\\ne0$, which is exactly the given domain.",
          "step": "1.2",
          "inputs": [
            "L1",
            "L2",
            "A1",
            "algebra"
          ]
        },
